<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<mxfile host="cli" modified="" agent="drawio-skill-cli" version="21.0.0">
  <diagram name="Page-1">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1120" dy="720" grid="1" gridSize="8" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1640" pageHeight="552" math="1" background="#FFFFFF"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="2" value="Define a Controlled Reasoning Task
Restrict proofs to chained modus ponens
Require one unique gold proof
Keep sentences easy to parse" style="shape=document;boundedLbl=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#9E9E9E;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#212121;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;verticalAlign=middle;align=center" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="-80" y="-8" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="3" value="Generate a Linear Ontology
Sample 3 to 10 concepts from a prior
Add subtype relations and properties
Give each node at most one child" style="shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=15;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#E8F5E9;strokeColor=#4CAF50;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#212121;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;verticalAlign=middle;align=center" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="160" y="-8" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="4" value="Choose the Ontology Condition
Fictional concept names
Real-world-consistent true ontologies
Random counterfactual false ontologies" style="rounded=1;arcSize=20;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#E3F2FD;strokeColor=#2196F3;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#212121;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;verticalAlign=middle;align=center" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="400" y="-8" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="5" value="Seed a Formal Proof
Choose a starting node uniformly
Assign one entity to that concept
Create the initial logical axiom" style="rounded=1;arcSize=20;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#E3F2FD;strokeColor=#2196F3;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#212121;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;verticalAlign=middle;align=center" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="640" y="-8" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="6" value="Traverse Up the Ontology
Apply one deduction rule per hop
Stop at the target node or property
Control 1 · 3 · 5 proof hops" style="rounded=1;arcSize=20;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#E3F2FD;strokeColor=#2196F3;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#212121;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;verticalAlign=middle;align=center" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="880" y="-8" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="7" value="Render the Natural-Language Context
Map every edge and property by grammar
Use syntactically simple variants
Preserve a unique inverse parse" style="shape=document;boundedLbl=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#9E9E9E;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#212121;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;verticalAlign=middle;align=center" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1120" y="-8" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="8" value="Control Context Difficulty
Add distractors to block shortcuts
Order facts top-down or bottom-up
Expose planning rather than retrieval" style="rounded=1;arcSize=20;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#E3F2FD;strokeColor=#2196F3;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#212121;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;verticalAlign=middle;align=center" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1360" y="-8" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="9" value="Create Query and Binary Label
State the proof's initial entity fact
Ask about conclusion or negation at 0.5
Label the item True or False" style="rounded=1;arcSize=20;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#E3F2FD;strokeColor=#2196F3;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#212121;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;verticalAlign=middle;align=center" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1360" y="368" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="10" value="Generate the Gold Chain of Thought
Translate each proof conclusion
Keep one sentence per formal step
Store context · query · CoT · label" style="shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=15;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#E8F5E9;strokeColor=#4CAF50;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#212121;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;verticalAlign=middle;align=center" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1120" y="368" width="200" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="11" value="Run Eight-Shot CoT Evaluation
Generate demonstrations independently
Append one test question without answer
